  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math> solid undergoes disproportionation reaction under alkaline conditions to form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p>Statement II: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo></msubsup></math> can undergo disproportionation reaction under acidic condition.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xnNhK",
      "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "5HUIk",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ggEEo",
      "text": "Both statement I and statement II are incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QQkxQ",
      "text": "Both statement I and statement II are correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A disproportionation reaction is a reaction in which the same element is simultaneously oxidized and reduced. In this type of reaction, a single substance gives two products, one is oxidized while the other is reduced.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>⊝</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>⊝</mo></msubsup></math> cannot undergo disproportionation reaction as chlorine is present in its highest oxidation state.</p><p>Hence, statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is correct and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is incorrect.</p>",
